@inherits PlaytestPanel
@* The board's region. Deliberately unframed: a border and a padding around the board is a border
   and a padding taken off the board, and the board is the screen. The panel's whole job is to hand
   the grid the box it fits itself into.

   Nothing in here is a row except the board. Three notices used to be — a refusal, the mid-run
   reload notice and the frozen-board line — and between them they took height off the position to
   say things a player reads once. They are toasts now, and the status band above them is an overlay
   for the same reason: the whole point of this region is that it is the board's. *@

<div class="battlefield @(ShowBoard ? string.Empty : "boardless")">
    @* Out of flow, over the board, top-centre. Nothing in this stack occupies a layout row, which
       is why the region's height is the same whether or not anything has something to say. *@
    <div class="overlays">
        <SystemToast />
        <StatusBand />
    </div>

    @if (ShowBoard)
    {
        <CoordinateGrid />
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="between">
            <h2>Between nodes</h2>
            <p class="dim">
                The run is standing between fights, so there is no board. What just happened is
                below, straight off the run's own events.
            </p>
            <ul class="run-events">
                @foreach (var e in Runs.LastEvents)
                {
                    <li>@RunEventText.Describe(e)</li>
                }
            </ul>
        </div>
    }
</div>

